            <history xml:id="history_id5f913b4b">
               <p xml:id="idm155">Sometime before 1875 Gade had given his publishing firm Fr. Kistner reason to believe that he was planning a new series of Aquarelles. However, they did not materialize until the summer of 1881, though Gade did not post the manuscript until 9 November to his two publishers: Wilhelm Hansen in Copenhagen and Fr. Kistner in Leipzig, they managed to have the printed items ready in time for Christmas.</p>
            </history>
